WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.370
- Here are five things
you probably need to hear.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.260
Number one,

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.930
not everything that happens
to you is your fault,

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.680
but everything that happens
to you is your responsibility.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.630
Right after that you
might think to yourself

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.230
everything is my responsibility.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:17.500
How is everything that happens
to me my responsibility?

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.350
I can't possibly account
for every little thing

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.800
that life throws my way,
the chaos, the triumph

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.620
and if something goes wrong,
which it inevitably will.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.630
Am I supposed to blame myself?

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.330
Because I was responsible

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.080
for having that thing not go wrong.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.960
That's not really what
I'm getting at here,

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.310
because for most of us,

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.290
our domain of influence is fairly small.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.670
We usually go to similar places,

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.214
we see similar people,

00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:46.060
we do similar activities
as we do most days.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.560
And occasionally we step outside the norm

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.560
and we experience new
people, places and things

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:52.980
to freshen things up.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:53.950
And along the way,

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:57.120
we'll be put in situations
that we don't like,

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.530
situations that make us
feel uncomfortable or angry.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:02.870
We'll talk to people
that we think are idiots.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.950
And occasionally we'll be blindsided

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.259
by tragedy or misfortune.

00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:09.610
I don't have to tell
you what life is like.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:13.360
Life is spicy, but if it is in our life,

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.767
it is our responsibility to figure out

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.700
what we're going to do about it.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.220
Because who else's responsibility is it?

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.730
Who else is responsible
for your physical fitness,

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.510
your mental health, your social life?

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:29.130
Who else is responsible
for the types of people

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.780
that you're inviting into your life?

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.480
The type of reaction that you have

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.060
when something doesn't go your way.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.610
When you break it down like this,

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.930
it's really hard to think of anything

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.060
that's not your responsibility.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.710
Anything that you would realistically do,

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:44.850
interact with, experience.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.780
Aren't you tired of
delegating the responsibility

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:50.150
of your own flourishing onto other people?

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.660
It's probably time that
you have some confidence

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.350
in your ability to make
decisions for yourself.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:59.300
To assume responsibility over
the outcomes of your life,

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.730
regardless of whose fault it may be.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.810
Because at the end of
the day, it affects you.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.360
So what are you gonna do about it?

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:09.200
Number two, life gets easier
when you're on your own side.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.938
If you love yourself first and
treat yourself with respect

00:02:12.938 --> 00:02:15.320
you'll have more love to give.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.730
When you dislike yourself
and treat yourself poorly,

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.143
then you'll start to subliminally

00:02:20.143 --> 00:02:22.860
feel unlikable and worthless.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.550
And if this is your default mode of being,

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.980
if you continue to treat yourself poorly,

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.120
if you don't like yourself very much,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.310
then every single
interaction that you have

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:35.620
with every single person in
your life will be tainted

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.260
with the need to solve
this inherent problem.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.600
Because we need to feel
loved and accepted.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.200
And if you starve yourself
of your own approval

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.600
off the get go,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.970
then every interaction
that we have with people

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.680
will be trying to gain that approval back.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.153
You'll start to rely
heavily on other people

00:02:52.153 --> 00:02:55.210
to make you feel validated
and worth something.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:56.540
And if you do this long enough

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:59.170
you'll start to lean on
this external validation

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:01.670
like a crutch, addicted to compliments,

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:05.120
constantly searching for
validation and approval.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.440
You'll start to wear clothes
that you don't necessarily like

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.300
but you think you're gonna get
a lot of compliments on it.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.880
You think you're being kind of
bold and brash by wearing it.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.660
And when you don't get that attention

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.497
that you so desperately require,

00:03:16.497 --> 00:03:18.400
you'll start to build resentment.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.090
You'll start to feel butt hurt.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.840
You'll be kind of passive
aggressive for no reason

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.130
because they owe you something, right?

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:28.210
Every interaction that
you have is an exchange,

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:29.550
you're nice to people,

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.040
you compliment people,

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.190
just so that you can be complimented back.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.130
And if people treat you poorly,

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.260
holy smokes, that ruins your day.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.900
Because when a person doesn't just not

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:39.920
return your compliment

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:41.200
but they're rude to you,

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.000
they become public enemy number one.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.620
Because you've conditioned yourself

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.110
to place your entire sense of self-worth

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:48.550
in the hands of other people.

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.730
But at the end of the day,

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:53.750
what you think other people
owe you, you owe to yourself.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.290
If you start treating
yourself like somebody

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.290
that you genuinely care
about and want the best for,

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:02.560
if you start acting as if
you're on your own side

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.550
then it will change every
single aspect of your life.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:08.110
It will change the way
you walk into a room.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:11.340
It will change the way that
you interact with other people.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.510
It will change the clothes that you wear,

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:14.980
the way that you speak,

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.800
and every decision that you make.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.894
when you treat yourself with
respect and you love yourself

00:04:19.894 --> 00:04:23.100
then you will actually be
able to give compliments

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.030
without expecting any in return.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.590
You will actually have
the ability to be generous

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:31.300
with your time, with your
attention, with your resources

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.060
because you genuinely want to,

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:35.200
it comes from a place of abundance.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:39.490
Treating yourself with respect,
just as a ridiculous ROI.

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:42.210
Number three, nobody owes you anything.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.920
You are not entitled to any job position,

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:47.520
any lifestyle, any relationship.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.190
Just because you have
big muscles and workout

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:52.610
doesn't mean you're entitled
to a hot girlfriend.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.700
Maybe your personality is the equivalent

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:57.050
of a wet sock or a dirty diaper.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:58.920
Just because you have a business degree

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.320
from a Community College,

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.640
doesn't mean that you're entitled

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:03.280
to be on the board of directors.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.450
Even if your business
degree is from Harvard

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.139
or some other prestigious school,

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:09.040
you're still not entitled to anything.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.780
The type of person who walks around

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.664
like the world owes them something,

00:05:12.664 --> 00:05:15.080
usually comes from a place of lack.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.680
And they're usually very ungrateful

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.200
when they get the thing that
they think they deserve.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.120
And they're white-hot and
vengeful when they don't get it.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:24.000
The type of person who thinks this way

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.800
usually has a giant ego.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.730
They have an idea of themselves

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:30.950
that is disconnected
from reality in some way.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.690
They probably have some
delusion of grandeur

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.510
where they want to appear on the surface

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:37.620
that they're better
than they actually are.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.360
But as I've covered in
previous videos, ego is brutal.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.160
It distorts you from the truth,

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:44.680
it stunts growth,

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:47.790
ego is far more concerned
with being somebody

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.310
rather than doing something.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:50.950
And if you followed step two

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.330
and started treating
yourself like somebody

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.080
you're responsible for helping,

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.830
which is kind of a direct
quote from Jordan Peterson,

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:59.700
then you wouldn't require others

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:02.370
to give you things to make you feel whole.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.540
You'll start to want certain positions

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:07.810
because of a genuine confidence
that you could add value.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:11.650
So instead of chasing status,
work on developing competence,

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:14.270
focus on the craft, not the corner office.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.240
Because 99 times out of a hundred,

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:18.310
your work will speak for itself.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.820
Number four, communism has
failed every time it was tried.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.450
Number five, it's going to be okay.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.477
I don't know what you're
going through right now.

00:06:26.477 --> 00:06:29.860
You could be having a
very great time in life.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:33.030
It could be, you know
probably the best time

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:33.863
that you've ever had.

00:06:33.863 --> 00:06:35.830
You might feel energetic and optimistic

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.180
and like everywhere you go,

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.453
there's a song singing behind you,

00:06:39.453 --> 00:06:40.940
a song singing behind you,

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:42.120
there's a background track,

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:46.240
cinematic score elevating
all of your steps,

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:47.863
butterflies everywhere.

00:06:47.863 --> 00:06:51.470
But for a lot of people, I know
that's indeed not the case.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:53.270
I get the feeling that
there's a lot of people

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:56.560
watching the video that
are in a very rough place.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.210
Maybe they're going through something

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:03.210
that is just like
incomprehensibly, tragic, you know.

00:07:03.318 --> 00:07:07.760
Life has a habit of doing
that to a lot of people.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.480
I know it's hard to think about,

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:15.200
it's hard to imagine that
things could be better for you.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.200
And sometimes it's not
better for a little while

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.110
but life's kinda weird

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:23.530
because it seems like every
dark period that I've ever had

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.124
in my life has always turned into a period

00:07:26.124 --> 00:07:31.080
where I looked back and I never
regretted the dark period.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.099
Like there was always so much to learn

00:07:34.099 --> 00:07:36.410
in those periods of darkness.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:40.600
So much to learn about
yourself, about other people.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:44.357
And sometimes those
realizations about other people

00:07:44.357 --> 00:07:48.850
are that people can be
pretty terrible. (laughs)

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:53.850
But I think that if you have
compassion for yourself,

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:56.114
if you have compassion for others,

00:07:56.114 --> 00:07:59.190
if you realize that at the end of the day

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:01.740
you're still responsible
for your own happiness,

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.668
regardless of whose fault

00:08:03.668 --> 00:08:05.990
your current happiness levels might be.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:09.000
You're still responsible
for making something of it

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.624
and there is always
something to be made from it.

00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:14.490
As long as you're voluntarily willing

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:17.040
to confront whatever your situation is in

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.270
with humility and perseverance,

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:22.030
something good always comes from it

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:23.250
and that's been my experience.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.340
The only time something
good doesn't come from it

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:28.500
is if you bury your head
in the sand and give up.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.440
But even then,

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:32.200
I feel like we're given
countless second chances in life.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.759
So if you are currently
burying your head in the sand,

00:08:35.759 --> 00:08:38.710
consider taking your head out of the sand,

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:41.100
looking around dusting yourself off

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.400
and getting back on the grind.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.244
Because at the end of the day,

00:08:45.244 --> 00:08:47.780
if you are willing to stick with it,

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:51.350
things will be okay,
they always will be okay.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:54.140
Even if you're not okay, that's okay too.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:55.133
It's gonna be okay.

